@section 13.6 | Polar and Ocean Missions

@q 16:15-17

India's Antarctic stations: **Dakshin Gangotri** (1983, the first, now a supply base), **Maitri** (1989) and **Bharati** (2012); **Himadri** (2008) is in the Arctic (Svalbard). **Samudrayaan**, under the **Deep Ocean Mission**, will take three people to **6,000 m** in the submersible **Matsya-6000**.

